#![enable(implicit_some)]
// A synthetic hull FITTED to the published form coefficients of the YD-41.
//
// It is NOT the YD-41's lines. The book publishes a lines drawing but no table
// of offsets, and scaling offsets off a drawing would put measurement error
// into the very thing meant to serve as an oracle. The offsets below come from
// a smooth parametric form whose knobs were fitted until its form coefficients
// matched Appendix 1's half-loaded column. Fitting geometry to published
// coefficients is a standard parametric-design operation; it is not a
// transcription, and nothing here should be quoted as the book's.
//
// Fit against Appendix 1 (half-loaded), measured analytically at the design
// waterline:
//     Cm  0.7150  vs 0.7150   (exact by construction)
//     Cp  0.5608  vs 0.5600   (0.14 %)
//     Cwp 0.7064  vs 0.7069   (-0.07 %)
//     LCB -4.19 %  vs -4.20 %
//     LCF -7.30 %  vs -7.30 %
//     Vc  6.069 m^3 vs 6.050   (0.31 %)
//     Aw  26.73 m^2 vs 26.75   (-0.07 %)
//
// Why it exists: the analytic test shapes (barge, half-cylinder) prove
// exactness but are prismatic and trivial. This is the only boat with geometry,
// so it is the only thing exercising loft -> clip -> hydrostatics -> flotation
// -> sectional areas end to end on a fair hull with rocker, a fine bow, a broad
// transom and flare. Being inside the DSYHS envelope it can also carry a
// resistance calculation, which its predecessor at Cp 0.63 could not.
//
// The keel line rises to 0.360 m at the stem, deliberately kept below the
// 0.40 m design draft: let it cross, and the canoe body emerges before the stem
// so the waterline is shorter than the file claims. The loader rejects that
// outright, which is how the first attempt at this hull was caught.
//
// Lwl 11.90 m, Bwl 3.18 m, BMAX 4.20 m, canoe body draft 0.40 m. Freeboard from
// Appendix 1's Ff/Lwl = 0.121 and Ff/Fa = 1.23. No appendages and no rig: only
// the hull was fitted, and inventing a keel to match would be exactly the
// fabrication this file exists to avoid. Use boats/yd41.ron for those.
//
// Frame: x forward from the aft perpendicular, y half-breadth, z up from the
// baseline. SI throughout.
